MIGUEL MELO is an Assistant Researcher with INESC TEC, specializing in computer graphics. He is also the Manager of the Multisensory Virtual Reality Laboratory MASSIVE. His research interests include computer graphics, HDR, and multisensory virtual reality. He is a member of the Executive Committee of Eurographics.
GUILHERME GONÇALVES received the bachelor’s degree from the University of Trás-os-Montes e Alto Douro (UTAD), Portugal, in 2015, where he is currently pursuing the M.Sc. degree in multimedia. Since 2018, he has been a Research Fellow with INESC TEC, Porto, Portugal. His research interest includes multisensory virtual reality.

JOSÉ VASCONCELOS-RAPOSO is a Full Professor with the Education and Psychology Department, University of Trás-os-Montes e Alto Douro, specializing in performance psychology. He is also a Senior Researcher with INESC TEC. His research interest includes the use of technology to improve human performance applied in sports and health care.
MAXIMINO BESSA received the Habilitation degree. He is an Associate Professor with the Department of Engineering, University of Trás-osMontes and Alto Douro (UTAD), Portugal. He has been a Senior Researcher with INESC TEC, since 2009, and the Director of the Multisensory Virtual Reality Laboratory MASSIVE. He has been a member of the Eurographics Association, since 2003, and the President of the Portuguese Computer Graphics Chapter.

